          {
            "citation": "PDF p.94 and p.95 · legal instrument (CONC 7.20.1R)",
            "statement": "CONC 7.20.1R, as set out in the legal instrument, applies where a borrower has failed to make a payment by the time it has fallen due under a regulated deferred payment credit agreement (a 'missed payment'). Once a missed payment has occurred, the firm must notify the borrower as soon as possible, and must provide the information required by the rule together. The rule is drafted as a duty on firms. However, the publication is signalled as a consultation-phase document with proposed changes and no published final rules. The provision should therefore be treated as a draft proposal and not as a binding obligation, and human review is required.",
